{"step_index":1383,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-21T19:56:40Z","thinking":"**Verifying WebView2 Rendering**\n\nI've checked the CSS for the `body` tag in `web/css/main.css`. It does indeed set `background: var(--bg-primary)`, which resolves to `#090A0E`. This confirms my initial hypothesis that the `WebView2` control is rendering the content correctly. The background check passed; it's looking good!\n\n\n**Confirming WPF Composition**\n\nI've got it! The `MainWindow.xaml` change (`AllowsTransparency=\"True\"`) and the code-behind (`this.Opacity = opacity;`) will perfectly fade the entire window, including the opaque HTML background, smoothly. WPF's composition is handling the alpha channel of the entire composited surface, which is fantastic news. I'm satisfied now. I am also making sure to check the shortcuts.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"replace_file_content","args":{"AllowMultiple":false,"Description":"Remove manual SetLayeredWindowAttributes to avoid conflict with WPF native transparency.","EndLine":79,"Instruction":"Disable SetLayeredWindowAttributes in SetTransparency","ReplacementContent":"        public bool SetTransparency(double opacity)\n        {\n            if (_hwnd == IntPtr.Zero) return false;\n            try\n            {\n                // Native WPF Opacity now handles transparency (AllowsTransparency=\"True\")\n                // We no longer call SetLayeredWindowAttributes to avoid conflicts.\n                _currentTransparency = opacity;\n                return true;\n            }\n            catch\n            {\n                return false;\n            }\n        }","StartLine":59,"TargetContent":"        public bool SetTransparency(double opacity)\n        {\n            if (_hwnd == IntPtr.Zero) return false;\n            try\n            {\n                EnableTransparencyStyle();\n                opacity = Math.Clamp(opacity, 0.1, 1.0);\n                _currentTransparency = opacity;\n                byte alpha = (byte)(opacity * 255);\n\n                bool res = NativeMethods.SetLayeredWindowAttributes(_hwnd, 0, alpha, NativeMethods.LWA_ALPHA);\n                return res;\n            }\n            catch\n            {\n                return false;\n            }\n        }","TargetFile":"c:\\Users\\Arthur Henrique\\Documents\\GitHub\\Spectra\\src-csharp\\Platform\\WindowManager.cs","toolAction":"Disabling Win32 Layered Window alpha to rely on WPF","toolSummary":"Update WindowManager.cs SetTransparency"}}]}
